{
  "meta": {
    "authoring": "Fable 5.1 bounded refinement of the earlier advisory plan. The earlier result is preserved unchanged as history; this message supersedes only the items listed in fixture_overrides. Still no R15 design, implementation, operational prompt or provider output has been supplied. No tools were used. No file was inspected or written.",
    "provenance": "This advisory design itself was produced by an actual Claude.ai Max subscription bridge invocation of Claude (Fable 5.1). What did NOT occur: any research, extraction or provider experiment against fixtures, any OpenRouter/API Claude call, any paid experiment, any run of an R15 implementation.",
    "data_status": "All examples are newly authored fictional test data, plus one outcome-exposed public regression pattern used as data only. Nothing is unseen-source evidence, an accuracy score or a model performance result.",
    "execution": "Pending. Codex executes approved offline tests only after an implementation is supplied. No implementation is proposed here."
  },
  "refined_test_plan_markdown": "# R15 Condition/Qualification Preservation — TEST-PLAN.md (Fable advisory, refined; execution pending)\n\n## Provenance\nAuthored via the Claude.ai Max bridge (Fable 5.1) as advisory design. No research/extraction provider experiment, no API/OpenRouter route, no paid experiment, no implementation run. Earlier advisory text is retained as history; this file is the current plan.\n\n## Purpose\nDiscriminate full preservation of supported conditions/qualifications from coherent-but-incomplete extraction, inversion, scope leakage, contradiction collapse and serialization clipping, in source-only semantic inventories. Representation is unspecified. Structural validity is never evidence of semantic completeness.\n\n## Oracle tiers\n- **Tier A — deterministic.** Runs only on authored fixtures whose expected atoms/operators/scopes carry an explicit, reviewed mapping from the implementation's representation to fixture atoms, and on known-bad outputs (regression shapes). Byte/hash checks apply to evidence spans and receipts only.\n- **Tier B — advisory.** Paraphrase entailment, normative force, scope ambiguity, materiality of uncovered spans, adequacy of uncertainty notes. Needs AI/human review even where metadata automates a known inversion or loss. Unseen-source completeness is always Tier B.\n- **Triage signals (neither tier's verdict).** Dangling punctuation, non-terminal fragments, trailing commas, empty strings, script-set differences. They queue a string for atom-level survival and advisory review; they are not semantic failures by themselves. No translation capability is required; a supported proper name or term in another script is acceptable when grounded.\n\n## Outcome vocabulary (per fixture, per atom; never summed)\n- PRESERVED — expected atoms, operators, scope targets, dimensions and references present, grounded, not inverted; contradictions and ambiguities carried explicitly.\n- BOUNDED-FAIL — explicit failure under the implementation's declared capacity policy (inclusive/exclusive/sentinel; per-unit or whole-inventory). No partial salvage, clipping or repair.\n- SILENT-LOSS — atom, operator, scope, dimension or reference absent or shortened with no failure signal.\n- INVERTED — operator, polarity, scope, modality or comparator contradicts the fixture.\n- COLLAPSED — a fixture-marked contradiction or ambiguity resolved to one reading without uncertainty.\n- FABRICATED — content not grounded in fixture bytes (resolved missing section, filled timezone, inferred status).\n- NOT-EXPOSED / POLICY-UNDECLARED — bound or capacity policy not declared; recorded, not scored.\n\n## Boundary rule\nFor each declared bound B, probe B-1, B, B+1 and interpret results by the declared inclusive/exclusive/sentinel policy. Exactly-B passing is not assumed. Global request/inventory limits may fail as whole-inventory BOUNDED-FAIL without naming a unit; per-unit limits should name the unit only if the implementation declares per-unit semantics. Local byte/char/token estimates are not matched-tokenizer or live-fit guarantees.\n\n## Reference rule\nA reference to content not in the supplied excerpt is UNAVAILABLE-IN-EXCERPT. That is not a jurisdictional/external legal classification. Unavailable references retain their target identifier and are not resolved. An invalid internal link is an inventory ID that points to no inventory node; it is a structural defect, distinct from an unavailable source reference. Waiver interaction with an unavailable requirement is UNKNOWN, not asserted either way.\n\n## Test families (12)\n| ID | Family | Fixtures | Tier A (automatic) | Tier B (advisory) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| TF-01 | Full vs coherent-but-incomplete conjunction | FX-A, FX-A2 | atom coverage; grammatical-prefix detection | paraphrase adequacy |\n| TF-02 | Boolean/operator inversion | FX-B, FX-A | operator per group; nesting shape | alternate encodings |\n| TF-03 | Baseline vs granted-waiver scope; nested exceptions | FX-A2, FX-B, FX-E | waiver trigger ≠ offer; waived-set equality | scope paraphrase |\n| TF-04 | Unavailable references vs invalid internal links | FX-B, FX-G, FX-S2 | unavailable marker + identifier; no resolution text; dangling-ID detection | reference-class choice where ambiguous |\n| TF-05 | Modal strength, bare imperative, contradiction | FX-C | label within allowed set; both statements present | justification of chosen force |\n| TF-06 | Proposed vs current status scope | FX-C, FX-C2 | status within allowed set per duty | scope-uncertainty wording |\n| TF-07 | Independent clock/date/tz/receipt dimensions | FX-D | per-dimension equality incl. ABSENT | added-inference labeling |\n| TF-08 | Unicode exact evidence and receipts | FX-F | evidence/receipt byte equality; no NFC collapse; declared offset unit; separator retention | paraphrase grounding |\n| TF-09 | Capacity bounds and payload growth | FX-L | outcome consistent with declared policy; no clipped strings; growth table | growth acceptability |\n| TF-10 | Receipts, coverage, truncation/receipt drift | FX-R, FX-A trunc | hash equality; span bounds; atom disappearance matches deletion | uncovered-span materiality |\n| TF-11 | Member-scoped permissions, exception leakage | FX-E | member×condition×exception matrix | sufficiency vs necessity labels |\n| TF-12 | Structure-only validity and regression string shapes | FX-S1, FX-REG | cycle/dangling/duplicate detection; triage flags; atom survival | whether a flagged string was the only carrier |\n\n## Execution notes (Codex, later)\n- `python -I`; fixtures in their own directory; scripts elsewhere; fixture bytes canonical.\n- Fixture files keep `source` (bytes) separate from `expected` (checker data). No test instructions inside `source`.\n- Contradiction variants require both statements plus uncertainty; coherent scope-change variants edit every conflicting sentence and require the new scope.\n",
  "fixture_overrides": {
    "FX-A": {
      "change": "Correct necessity claim and waiver-trigger ambiguity; split waiver-scope mutation into contradiction vs coherent variants. Source unchanged.",
      "expected_replacement": {
        "permission": "district MAY collect enrollment fee ('may ... only')",
        "baseline_conditions": ["A1 eligible district", "A2 child enrolled in classroom receiving state funding", "A3 published sliding schedule", "A4 written notice in accessible language", "A5 hardship review offered without application fee", "A6 collections separately recorded by program year"],
        "necessity": "A1, A2, A4, A5, A6 necessary wherever stated; A3 necessary absent a waiver. The source says 'the hardship review waives the published-schedule condition only' but does not state what event constitutes waiver (offering a review (A5), conducting it, or granting relief). Record trigger as AMBIGUOUS; an inventory may adopt a justified reading with explicit uncertainty. Asserting A3 unconditionally necessary, or asserting A3 waived whenever A5 holds, is COLLAPSED.",
        "exclusions": ["X1 eligible-not-placed Program Oak", "X2 eligible-not-placed Program Pine", "X3 child with disability entitled to FAPE"],
        "operator_X": "OR; Oak/Pine disjunction inside X1/X2",
        "waiver_scope": {"waives_exactly": ["A3"], "does_not_waive": ["X1", "X2", "X3", "A6"], "unknown_interaction": ["A1", "A2", "A4", "A5"], "note": "'only' supports non-waiver of the others, but list them as UNKNOWN-INTERACTION rather than asserted non-waiver."}
      },
      "variants_replacement_for": {
        "A-waiver-leak": "REMOVED; replaced by the two below.",
        "A-waiver-contradiction": {"spec": "Replace 'waives the published-schedule condition only' with 'waives the published-schedule and separate-accounting conditions'; keep the following clause 'it does not waive the no-fee protections or the separate-accounting condition' intact.", "expect": "Both statements present; A6 waiver status marked CONTRADICTORY with uncertainty. Choosing either reading silently is COLLAPSED. Tier A: presence of both; Tier B: flag quality."},
        "A-waiver-scope-coherent": {"spec": "Replace the final sentence entirely with 'The hardship review waives the published-schedule and separate-accounting conditions only; it does not waive the no-fee protections.'", "expect": "waives_exactly = [A3, A6]; does_not_waive = [X1, X2, X3]; A6 not in does_not_waive. Tier A set equality."}
      },
      "unchanged": ["A-prefix-grammatical", "A-drop-independent", "A-and-to-or", "A-long-clause", "A-dup-shared", "A-trunc-source"]
    },
    "FX-A2": {
      "new": true,
      "families": ["TF-01", "TF-03"],
      "source": "An eligible district may collect an enrollment fee only for a child enrolled in a classroom receiving state funding, and only if the district has published a sliding schedule, has given the family written notice in an accessible language, has offered the family a hardship review without requiring an application fee, and separately records collections by program year. No fee may be charged to a child eligible for but not yet placed in Program Oak or Program Pine, or to a child with a disability entitled to free appropriate public education. If the district's hardship review board has issued a written hardship waiver to a family, the published-schedule condition does not apply to that family's fee; every other condition and the no-fee protections continue to apply to that family. Offering a hardship review does not by itself constitute a waiver.",
      "expected": {
        "baseline_unwaived": "fee permitted for a child only if A1..A6 all hold and no X1..X3 applies (same atom labels as FX-A)",
        "waiver_trigger": "W = hardship review board has issued a written hardship waiver to the family (distinct from A5 offering a review; source states offering ≠ waiver)",
        "waived_state": "when W holds for a family: A3 not required for that family; A1, A2, A4, A5, A6 still required; X1..X3 still block",
        "scope_of_waiver": "per family, not district-wide",
        "necessity_summary": "A3 is necessary iff not W; representation free (e.g., (A3 OR W) under the conjunction, or baseline/waived state pair); an inventory listing A3 as unconditionally necessary with no waiver link is SILENT-LOSS; one treating A5 as W is INVERTED",
        "evidence_spans": ["and only if the district has published a sliding schedule", "has issued a written hardship waiver to a family, the published-schedule condition does not apply", "every other condition and the no-fee protections continue to apply", "Offering a hardship review does not by itself constitute a waiver"]
      },
      "variants": [
        {"v": "A2-trigger-conflate", "spec": "Delete the last sentence.", "expect": "Trigger still W (issued written waiver) from the third sentence; absence of the clarifier does not license A5=W. Tier A: trigger atom = W."},
        {"v": "A2-scope-contradiction", "spec": "Change 'the published-schedule condition does not apply' to 'the published-schedule and separate-accounting conditions do not apply'; keep 'every other condition ... continue to apply' intact.", "expect": "A6 status under W marked CONTRADICTORY; both statements present. COLLAPSED if resolved silently."},
        {"v": "A2-scope-coherent", "spec": "Same edit plus change 'every other condition' to 'every other condition except separate accounting'.", "expect": "waived under W = [A3, A6]; still required = [A1, A2, A4, A5]; X unchanged. Tier A."},
        {"v": "A2-district-wide-leak", "spec": "Replace 'to that family's fee' with 'to any fee collected by the district'.", "expect": "scope_of_waiver = district-wide. Tier A."}
      ],
      "checks": {"automatic": ["baseline atom coverage", "W ≠ A5", "waived-set and still-required-set equality", "scope per family"], "advisory": ["acceptability of chosen waiver representation"]}
    },
    "FX-B": {
      "change": "Separate unknown waiver interaction from asserted non-override; reclassify section 7; split overreach into contradiction vs coherent variants.",
      "expected_replacement": {
        "eligibility": "A AND (B OR C) AND NOT(D AND NOT E) AND approval(section 7)",
        "operators": {"A_group": "AND", "BC_group": "OR", "nesting": "B OR C nested under AND"},
        "waiver_E": {"overrides": ["D"], "does_not_override_stated": ["A", "(B OR C)"], "unknown_interaction": ["section 7 approval"]},
        "section_7": {"status": "UNAVAILABLE-IN-EXCERPT", "identifier_retained": "section 7", "must_not": "resolve, classify as external/jurisdictional, or assert satisfied/unsatisfied"}
      },
      "variants_replacement_for": {
        "B-waiver-overreach": "REMOVED; replaced by the two below.",
        "B-override-contradiction": {"spec": "Replace 'E overrides D only' with 'E overrides D and A'; keep 'it does not override A or the requirement that B or C hold' intact.", "expect": "Both present; A override status CONTRADICTORY with uncertainty; COLLAPSED if one reading chosen silently."},
        "B-override-scope-coherent": {"spec": "Replace the third sentence entirely with 'E overrides D and A only; it does not override the requirement that B or C hold.'", "expect": "overrides = [D, A]; does_not_override_stated = [(B OR C)]; unknown_interaction = [section 7]. Tier A."}
      },
      "unchanged": ["B-or-to-and", "B-paren-shift", "B-contradiction", "B-nesting-depth"]
    },
    "FX-C": {
      "change": "Allow justified force interpretation with explicit ambiguity for C4; record status-scope uncertainty instead of a blanket proposed label.",
      "expected_replacement": {
        "duties": [
          {"d": "C1 submit annual records", "modal": "must", "condition": "served >20 participants AND received state funds", "status": "proposed (explicit via opening phrase in same sentence)"},
          {"d": "C2 may submit records voluntarily", "modal": "may", "condition": "receives only private funds", "status": "proposed or scope-uncertain (same sentence as opening phrase; both accepted)"},
          {"d": "C3 retain supporting worksheets", "modal": "should", "status": "allowed: proposed | scope-uncertain; forbidden: current/in-force asserted"},
          {"d": "C4 send requests to the office by the stated date", "modal": "allowed: unspecified | mandatory-with-explicit-ambiguity | advisory-with-explicit-ambiguity | imperative-unlabeled; forbidden: any force label without an ambiguity marker, or discarding the directive", "deadline_ref": "'the stated date' UNAVAILABLE-IN-EXCERPT or internal-unresolved; identifier retained; no date fabricated", "status": "allowed: proposed | scope-uncertain"}
        ],
        "status_rule": "The opening phrase clearly scopes C1; its reach over C2–C4 is ambiguous. Asserting 'current' for any duty is FABRICATED; asserting 'proposed' for C3/C4 without uncertainty is accepted as a justified reading only if the inventory records the scope basis; blanket proposed is not required."
      },
      "variants_unchanged": ["C-modal-swap", "C-current-vs-proposed", "C-contradictory-modality", "C-threshold"],
      "variant_note": "C-current-vs-proposed sub-variant 2 (prefix deleted): allowed status = unspecified for all four; 'proposed' then FABRICATED."
    },
    "FX-C2": {
      "new": true,
      "families": ["TF-06"],
      "source": "Each of the following four requirements is part of the proposed rule and is not currently in effect. First, organizations must submit annual records if they served more than twenty participants and received state funds. Second, organizations receiving only private funds may submit records voluntarily. Third, organizations should retain supporting worksheets. Fourth, organizations send requests to the office by the stated date.",
      "expected": {
        "status": "proposed for all four, explicit; 'not currently in effect' preserved as a separate fact",
        "modals": {"C1": "must", "C2": "may", "C3": "should", "C4": "bare imperative; allowed labels as in FX-C C4"},
        "operator_C1": "AND",
        "comparator": ">20 strict"
      },
      "variants": [
        {"v": "C2-partial-scope", "spec": "Change 'Each of the following four requirements' to 'The first two of the following requirements'.", "expect": "C1, C2 proposed; C3, C4 status unspecified. Tier A allowed-set."},
        {"v": "C2-status-contradiction", "spec": "Append 'The third requirement is currently in effect.' leaving the opening sentence intact.", "expect": "C3 status CONTRADICTORY, both statements present."}
      ],
      "checks": {"automatic": ["status per duty", "modal per duty within allowed set", "AND and comparator"], "advisory": ["C4 force justification"]}
    },
    "FX-F": {
      "change": "Supply literal codepoint/byte data; separator generation data; clarify byte tests apply to evidence/receipts, not paraphrases.",
      "source_literal": {
        "line_text_json": "Caf\u00e9 / Cafe\u0301 / \u4e2d\u6587 / \ud83e\udee7",
        "tokens": [
          {"label": "cafe_precomposed", "codepoints": ["U+0043", "U+0061", "U+0066", "U+00E9"], "utf8_hex": "43 61 66 C3 A9", "utf16_units": 4},
          {"label": "cafe_decomposed", "codepoints": ["U+0043", "U+0061", "U+0066", "U+0065", "U+0301"], "utf8_hex": "43 61 66 65 CC 81", "utf16_units": 5},
          {"label": "zhongwen", "codepoints": ["U+4E2D", "U+6587"], "utf8_hex": "E4 B8 AD E6 96 87", "utf16_units": 2},
          {"label": "bubbles", "codepoints": ["U+1FAE7"], "utf8_hex": "F0 9F AB A7", "utf16_units": 2, "utf16_hex": "D83E DEE7"}
        ],
        "separator_token": " / (U+0020 U+002F U+0020)"
      },
      "separator_variant_generation": {
        "lines": [
          "L1: Caf\u00e9 / Cafe\u0301 / \u4e2d\u6587 / \ud83e\udee7",
          "L2: The fee applies only if the family has received written notice",
          "L3: in an accessible language, and",
          "L4: only if a hardship review was offered.",
          "L5: No fee for a child entitled to free appropriate public education."
        ],
        "separators_in_order": [
          {"after": "L1", "name": "CRLF", "codepoints": ["U+000D", "U+000A"], "utf8_hex": "0D 0A"},
          {"after": "L2", "name": "LF", "codepoints": ["U+000A"], "utf8_hex": "0A"},
          {"after": "L3", "name": "LINE SEPARATOR", "codepoints": ["U+2028"], "utf8_hex": "E2 80 A8"},
          {"after": "L4", "name": "PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR", "codepoints": ["U+2029"], "utf8_hex": "E2 80 A9"},
          {"after": "L5", "name": "NEL", "codepoints": ["U+0085"], "utf8_hex": "C2 85"}
        ],
        "planted_qualification": "L2–L4 form one condition group ('only if ... notice ... accessible language, and only if ... hardship review') spanning LF and U+2028 boundaries"
      },
      "expected_replacement": {
        "byte_tests_apply_to": ["evidence spans (quoted source)", "receipts (hash of bytes fed)"],
        "byte_tests_do_not_apply_to": "grounded paraphrases; a paraphrase must point to a grounded span and is judged for adequacy in Tier B",
        "no_nfc_collapse": "cafe_precomposed and cafe_decomposed remain distinct in evidence; one byte form emitted for both occurrences is a normalization failure",
        "offset_unit": "declared unit required; sidecar gives byte/codepoint/UTF-16 offsets; bubbles deltas (4/1/2) classify confusion",
        "separator_retention": "evidence spanning L2→L3→L4 must contain 0A and E2 80 A8 exactly; the condition group must be preserved whole or BOUNDED-FAIL per declared policy"
      },
      "variants_unchanged": ["F-nfc-bait", "F-offset-probe", "F-crlf-bomb (now specified by separator_variant_generation)"]
    },
    "FX-G": {
      "change": "Concrete two-referrer fictional source; test instructions removed from source; expectations separated.",
      "source": "4(a) A permit application fee of forty dollars applies to each application. 4(b) The fee in 4(a) is waived for an applicant who qualifies for the fee exemption described in section 99. 6(c) An applicant claiming the section 99 fee exemption must attach the exemption certificate to the application. Section 99 is not reproduced in this notice.",
      "expected": {
        "facts": ["G0 fee $40 per application (4(a))", "G1 fee waived if applicant qualifies for section 99 exemption (4(b)) — condition content unavailable", "G2 claimant of section 99 exemption must attach exemption certificate (6(c))"],
        "reference": {"identifier": "section 99", "status": "UNAVAILABLE-IN-EXCERPT (source states not reproduced)", "referrers": ["G1", "G2"], "many_to_many": "both referrers link to the one unavailable target; duplicating the target node is acceptable; two different targets or a resolved target is not"},
        "must_not": ["invent exemption criteria", "mark G1 waiver satisfied/unsatisfied", "treat G2's certificate duty as the exemption criteria", "emit a bare 'unknown' that drops the identifier 'section 99'", "classify section 99 as external/jurisdictional law"]
      },
      "variants": [
        {"v": "G-partial-supply", "spec": "Append 'Section 99. The fee exemption applies to an applicant whose household' (cut mid-phrase).", "expect": "Partial content preserved as partial; not completed; G1/G2 still link to section 99 now partially available. Tier A prefix check; Tier B labeling."},
        {"v": "G-internal-vs-external", "spec": "Add '4(c) Applicants under paragraph 4(b) must also meet the residency condition in 4(d). 4(d) The applicant must reside in the district.' so 4(d) is an in-excerpt reference.", "expect": "4(d) resolved in-excerpt; section 99 remains unavailable; a dangling inventory ID (if any) reported structurally, separately. Tier A."}
      ],
      "checks": {"automatic": ["identifier retained", "two referrers → one target", "no exemption text absent from source", "in-excerpt resolution"], "advisory": ["plausibility audit of any explanatory text"]}
    },
    "FX-S2": {
      "change": "Reclassify reference classes.",
      "expected_replacement": {
        "classes": {"the stated date": "unresolved; allowed: unavailable-in-excerpt | internal-unresolved, with uncertainty", "section 99": "UNAVAILABLE-IN-EXCERPT", "section 7": "UNAVAILABLE-IN-EXCERPT", "paragraph 2": "in-excerpt resolved"},
        "forbidden": ["resolving unavailable targets", "generic 'unknown' discarding the identifier", "jurisdictional/external legal classification from absence alone", "confusing an invalid inventory link (dangling ID) with an unavailable source reference"]
      }
    },
    "FX-REG": {
      "change": "Downgrade string-health flags to triage signals; no forced translation; proper names in other scripts allowed.",
      "expected_checker_behaviour_replacement": {
        "triage": "Each of the five planted strings is queued (dangling terminator, non-terminal fragment, script outside source script set, trailing comma, empty). Queueing is not a verdict.",
        "atom_survival": "For each queued string, map to its atom (A3, A5) via the reviewed mapping and report SURVIVES-ELSEWHERE vs ONLY-CARRIER-AFFECTED. Absence is judged per atom.",
        "script_rule": "A string in a script not present in the source is a triage signal only. If it is a grounded proper name, term, or a marked translation/paraphrase pointing to a source span, it is not a failure. The checker must not require translation capability.",
        "punctuation_rule": "Trailing comma / dangling conjunction is a triage signal; the string is then compared to its grounded span for prefix-truncation (Tier A) and adequacy (Tier B)."
      },
      "variants_unchanged": ["REG-grammatical-break", "REG-translation-marked"],
      "variant_added": {"v": "REG-proper-name-script", "spec": "Source contains the fictional proper name 'Program オーク' as a program title; output carries it verbatim.", "expect": "Queued by script signal, cleared as grounded proper name. Tier A grounding."}
    },
    "FX-L": {
      "change": "Follow declared capacity policy; no exactly-B pass assumption; no unit-naming requirement for global limits.",
      "expected_replacement": {
        "policy_first": "Before scoring, record the implementation's declared policy per bound: inclusive/exclusive/sentinel; per-unit vs whole-inventory; failure signal shape. If undeclared, record POLICY-UNDECLARED and run probes descriptively.",
        "at_B-1_B_B+1": "Acceptable outcomes at each probe are PRESERVED or BOUNDED-FAIL consistent with the declared policy. Whether exactly-B passes is determined by the declared inclusive/exclusive rule, not assumed.",
        "global_limits": "For request/inventory-wide limits, an explicit whole-inventory BOUNDED-FAIL is acceptable without naming a unit. Unit-named failure is expected only where the implementation declares per-unit limits.",
        "never_acceptable": ["shortened or repaired qualification strings", "partial salvage of an inventory presented as complete", "false completeness markers after a limit hit"],
        "payload_growth": "report output bytes / source bytes per probe; growth is recorded, not scored; a cliff near a bound is a Tier B note",
        "token_caveat": "local byte/char/token estimates are not matched-tokenizer or live output-fit guarantees"
      },
      "variants_replacement": [{"v": "L-undeclared", "spec": "No bound or policy declared.", "expect": "NOT-EXPOSED / POLICY-UNDECLARED; escalating offline probes (1k/4k/16k/64k bytes) recorded descriptively; any clipped string is still a failure."}]
    }
  },
  "oracle_limits": [
    "Tier A automation of operator/atom truth matrices applies only to authored logical fixtures (FX-A, FX-A2, FX-B, FX-C/C2 operators and comparators, FX-D dimensions, FX-E matrix, FX-G/S2 reference classes) and to known-bad output shapes (FX-REG), and only after an explicit reviewed mapping from the implementation's representation to fixture atoms exists. Without that mapping the fixture is run descriptively.",
    "Byte/hash equality is an oracle for evidence spans and receipts only. Accurate grounded paraphrases are not required to be byte-identical; their adequacy is Tier B.",
    "Generic paraphrase entailment, normative force of bare imperatives, status-scope reach of an opening phrase, waiver-trigger readings in FX-A, and materiality of uncovered spans are advisory and need AI/human review.",
    "Script-set differences, trailing punctuation, fragments and empty strings are triage signals that route a string to atom-survival and advisory review; they are not universal semantic failures. No translation capability is required; supported proper names in other scripts are accepted when grounded.",
    "Contradiction and ambiguity fixtures are scored on presence of both statements plus an uncertainty marker; the wording or form of that marker is advisory.",
    "Capacity probes are interpreted only under the implementation's declared policy; absence of a declaration yields POLICY-UNDECLARED, not pass or fail.",
    "Unavailable references are judged on identifier retention and non-resolution; the checker does not and cannot determine legal/jurisdictional status of missing sections.",
    "No aggregate score, accuracy denominator or model performance claim is produced; all verdicts are per fixture, per atom.",
    "Unseen-source (Tier B discovery) completeness is never automated by this plan."
  ],
  "unresolved_implementation_choices": [
    "Representation of qualifications (quoted span, paraphrase, logical form, graph, baseline/waived state pairs) and the reviewed mapping to fixture atoms.",
    "Declared capacity policy per bound: which bounds exist, inclusive/exclusive/sentinel, per-unit vs whole-inventory, failure signal shape.",
    "Offset unit (byte/codepoint/UTF-16) and receipt hash algorithm; whether receipts hash pre- or post-chunking bytes.",
    "How contradictions, ambiguity (bare imperative force, status scope, waiver trigger) and unavailable references are expressed — presence is automatic, form is advisory.",
    "Whether shared conditions and shared unavailable targets are linked many-to-many or duplicated per referrer; link-set equality is what is checked.",
    "Whether a merged unit (e.g., A1+A2) counts as preserving both atoms — default accept if both are recoverable from the grounded span, otherwise advisory.",
    "Whether 'proposed' status is per-assertion or document-level in the implementation; both accepted if each duty's allowed status set is satisfied.",
    "Reviewer selection for Tier B (AI on the Claude.ai Max bridge vs human); requires separate authorization and is out of scope here."
  ],
  "status": "Fable 5.1 bounded advisory refinement produced via the Claude.ai Max bridge. Earlier advisory preserved as history. No research/extraction provider experiment occurred. No fixture files written. Execution pending supply of an implementation; Codex to execute approved offline tests."
}

